  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_006 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) at 0.5176 acc, a large jump over config_049 (same encoders, singleprofile, no aggregation, concat) at 0.4348. However, that jump conflates multiprofile with the introduction of avgpool aggregation, so we cannot yet tell whether aggregation method itself is a meaningful lever. Config_009 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, transformer, concat) changes exactly one factor relative to config_006: aggregation from avgpool to transformer, while keeping the same RNA encoder, image encoder, profile setting, and fusion method. This isolates the effect of aggregation expressiveness. If transformer aggregation matches or exceeds avgpool, it suggests the multiprofile gain is robust to aggregation choice and we can focus on other axes (fusion, encoders). If it underperforms, avgpool is confirmed as the better compressor and we can exploit that. Under a tight budget, this single-factor comparison from the best-known configuration is the most information-dense next step."
